      ":question/problem": "![](images/50/50c8744e11960229d98ee0c3011fb9cdf80d1f7688468101871de590e66b48a1.png)\n\nIn the diagram above, $\u25b3PQR$ is isosceles and $QA^(\u2015)\u22a5PR^(\u2015)$.\n\nConsider the following statement:\n\n> $\u25b3QAP\u2245\u25b3QAR$\n\nThe table below gives the proof of the statement. Select the correct options in the table and thus complete the proof.\n\n|  | Statement | Reason |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| 1 | $\u25b3PQR$ is isosceles | Given |\n| 2 | {{field-1}} | Given |\n| 3 | $m\u2220QAP$ and $m\u2220QAR$ are right angles | Definition of perpendicular lines |\n| 4 | $QP^(\u2015)\u2245QR^(\u2015)$ | Definition of isosceles triangle |\n| 5 | {{field-2}} | {{field-3}} |\n| 6 | $\u25b3QAP\u2245\u25b3QAR$ | {{field-4}} |"
