      ":question/problem": "![](images/f8/f8c1f82aeb8dfd081c55741afe3b5362bc40d1569454addb17dc209fd13962e4.png)\n\nIn the diagram above, $PQ^(\u2015)$ bisects both $\u2220RPS$ and $\u2220RQS$.\n\nConsider the following statement:\n\n> $\u25b3PQR\u2245\u25b3PQS$\n\nThe table below provides proof of the statement. Select the correct options to complete the proof.\n\n|  | Statement | Reason |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| 1 | $PQ^(\u2015)$ bisects $\u2220RPS$ | {{field-1}} |\n| 2 | $\u2220RPQ\u2245\u2220SPQ$ | {{field-2}} |\n| 3 | $PQ^(\u2015)$ bisects $\u2220RQS$ | {{field-3}} |\n| 4 | $\u2220RQP\u2245\u2220SQP$ | {{field-4}} |\n| 5 | $PQ^(\u2015)\u2245PQ^(\u2015)$ | {{field-5}} |\n| 6 | $\u25b3PQR\u2245\u25b3PQS$ | {{field-6}} |"
